Subject: [PATCH] wifi: wl12xx: bind the wl127x / wl128x devices of the SPI glue

wlcore's SPI glue (wlcore/spi.c) creates the core platform device with
the chip family name, "wl127x" or "wl128x" for the wl12xx chips, while
the SDIO glue always uses "wl12xx". wl12xx only matches "wl12xx", so on
SPI nothing binds: the glue probes ("selected chip family is wl127x")
and then nothing happens, no wlan0 and no error. Seen on the Nokia N8
(TI WL1271 PG2.0 on SPI).

Match the two SPI names as well.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
  drivers/net/wireless/ti/wl12xx/main.c | 3 +++
  1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ti/wl12xx/main.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ti/wl12xx/main.c
index b26d42b4e..fa6c3ff84 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ti/wl12xx/main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ti/wl12xx/main.c
@@ -1933,6 +1933,9 @@ static void wl12xx_remove(struct platform_device *pdev)
 
 static const struct platform_device_id wl12xx_id_table[] = {
 	{ "wl12xx", 0 },
+	/* the spi glue names the platform device after the chip family */
+	{ "wl127x", 0 },
+	{ "wl128x", 0 },
 	{  } /* Terminating Entry */
 };
 MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(platform, wl12xx_id_table);
